{"id":"mahabharata-5-023","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":23,"title":"त्रयोविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 23 · Sanjaya at Upaplavya","summary":{"en":"Sanjaya reaches Upaplavya and greets Yudhishthira, who asks warmly after all the Kurus, the elders, teachers, women and servants. Yudhishthira says that no single good deed suffices, and asks what message Sanjaya brings.","kn":"ಸಂಜಯನು ಉಪಪ್ಲವ್ಯ ತಲುಪಿ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನಿಗೆ ನಮಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಎಲ್ಲ ಕುರುಗಳು, ಹಿರಿಯರು, ಗುರುಗಳು, ಸ್ತ್ರೀಯರು, ಸೇವಕರ ಕುಶಲವನ್ನು ಆತ್ಮೀಯತೆಯಿಂದ ವಿಚಾರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಒಂದೇ ಸತ್ಕಾರ್ಯ ಸಾಲದು ಎಂದು ಹೇಳಿ ಸಂಜಯನು ಯಾವ ಸಂದೇಶ ತಂದಿದ್ದಾನೆಂದು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"सञ्जय उपप्लव्य पहुँचकर युधिष्ठिर को प्रणाम करते हैं, जो स्नेह से सब कुरुओं, बड़ों, गुरुओं, स्त्रियों और सेवकों का कुशल पूछते हैं। युधिष्ठिर कहते हैं कि अकेला एक सत्कर्म पर्याप्त नहीं, और पूछते हैं कि सञ्जय क्या सन्देश लाए हैं।","te":"సంజయుడు ఉపప్లావ్యం చేరి యుధిష్ఠిరునికి నమస్కరిస్తాడు; యుధిష్ఠిరుడు కురువులందరి, పెద్దల, గురువుల, స్త్రీల, సేవకుల కుశలం ఆప్యాయంగా అడుగుతాడు. ఒక్క సత్కార్యం చాలదని చెప్పి సంజయుడు ఏ సందేశం తెచ్చాడని అడుగుతాడు.","ta":"ஸஞ்ஜயன் உபப்லவ்யத்தை அடைந்து யுதிஷ்டிரரை வணங்க, யுதிஷ்டிரர் எல்லாக் குருக்கள், மூத்தோர், ஆசிரியர்கள், பெண்கள், பணியாளர்களின் நலத்தையும் அன்புடன் விசாரிக்கிறார். ஒரு நற்செயல் மட்டும் போதாது என்று சொல்லி, ஸஞ்ஜயன் என்ன செய்தி கொணர்ந்துள்ளான் என்று கேட்கிறார்.","ml":"സഞ്ജയൻ ഉപപ്ലവ്യത്തിലെത്തി യുധിഷ്ഠിരനെ അഭിവാദ്യം ചെയ്യുന്നു; എല്ലാ കൗരവരെയും, മുതിർന്നവരെയും, ഗുരുക്കന്മാരെയും, സ്ത്രീകളെയും, ഭൃത്യന്മാരെയും കുറിച്ച് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ സ്നേഹത്തോടെ അന്വേഷിക്കുന്നു. ഒരൊറ്റ നല്ല പ്രവൃത്തി മതിയാകില്ലെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ പറയുന്നു; സഞ്ജയൻ കൊണ്ടുവന്ന സന്ദേശമെന്തെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം ചോദിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.23; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"संजययानपर्व","titleEn":"Sanjayayana Parva (Sanjaya's embassy)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"राज्ञस्तु वचनं श्रुत्वा धृतराष्ट्रस्य संजयः ।\nउपप्लव्यं ययौ द्रष्टुं पाण्डवानमितौजसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing King Dhritarashtra's words, Sanjaya went to see the Pandavas of immeasurable power at Upaplavya."}},{"n":2,"text":"स तु राजानमासाद्य धर्मात्मानं युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nप्रणिपत्य ततः पूर्वं सूतपुत्रोऽभ्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching the righteous King Yudhishthira, the charioteer's son first bowed to him and then spoke."}},{"n":3,"text":"गावल्गणिः संजयः सूतसूनु-\nरजातशत्रुमवदत्प्रतीतः ।\nदिष्ट्या राजंस्त्वामरोगं प्रपश्ये\nसहायवन्तं च महेन्द्रकल्पम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, son of Gavalgana and of a charioteer, said confidently to the king who had no enemies: By good fortune, O king, I see you free of illness, with allies, like Mahendra."}},{"n":4,"text":"अनामयं पृच्छति त्वाम्बिकेयो\nवृद्धो राजा धृतराष्ट्रो मनीषी ।\nकच्चिद्भीमः कुशली पाण्डवाग्र्यो\nधनंजयस्तौ च माद्रीतनूजौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The old king, wise Dhritarashtra, son of Ambika, asks after your health: Is Bhima well, the chief of the Pandavas, and Dhananjaya and the two sons of Madri?"}},{"n":5,"text":"कच्चित्कृष्णा द्रौपदी राजपुत्री\nसत्यव्रता वीरपत्नी सपुत्रा ।\nमनस्विनी यत्र च वाञ्छसि त्व-\nमिष्टान्कामान्भारत स्वस्तिकामः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And is Krishna Draupadi, the princess, true to her vows, wife of heroes, with her sons, and high-spirited, well, and do you have, Bharata, all the wishes you desire, wishing you welfare?"}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"गावल्गणे संजय स्वागतं ते\nप्रीतात्माहं त्वाभिवदामि सूत ।\nअनामयं प्रतिजाने तवाहं\nसहानुजैः कुशली चास्मि विद्वन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Welcome, Sanjaya, son of Gavalgana; I greet you gladly, charioteer. I assure you of your health, and I am well, wise one, with my younger brothers."}},{"n":7,"text":"चिरादिदं कुशलं भारतस्य\nश्रुत्वा राज्ञः कुरुवृद्धस्य सूत ।\nमन्ये साक्षाद्दृष्टमहं नरेन्द्रं\nदृष्ट्वैव त्वां संजय प्रीतियोगात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"After a long time, hearing news of the well-being of the Bharata king, the old Kuru, I feel, Sanjaya, that I have seen the king himself, from joy, just by seeing you."}},{"n":8,"text":"पितामहो नः स्थविरो मनस्वी\nमहाप्राज्ञः सर्वधर्मोपपन्नः ।\nस कौरव्यः कुशली तात भीष्मो\nयथापूर्वं वृत्तिरप्यस्य कच्चित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Is our grandfather, the old, spirited, very wise Bhishma, endowed with all dharma, well, the Kaurava? And is his way of life as before?"}},{"n":9,"text":"कच्चिद्राजा धृतराष्ट्रः सपुत्रो\nवैचित्रवीर्यः कुशली महात्मा ।\nमहाराजो बाह्लिकः प्रातिपेयः\nकच्चिद्विद्वान्कुशली सूतपुत्र ॥","meaning":{"en":"Is King Dhritarashtra, son of Vichitravirya, great-souled, well with his sons? Is the great king Bahlika, son of Pratipa, learned and well, charioteer's son?"}},{"n":10,"text":"स सोमदत्तः कुशली तात कच्चि-\nद्भूरिश्रवाः सत्यसंधः शलश्च ।\nद्रोणः सपुत्रश्च कृपश्च विप्रो\nमहेष्वासाः कच्चिदेतेऽप्यरोगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Is Somadatta well, and Bhurishravas, true to his word, and Shala? Are Drona with his son, and the Brahmin Kripa, those great archers, free of illness?"}},{"n":11,"text":"महाप्राज्ञाः सर्वशास्त्रावदाता\nधनुर्भृतां मुख्यतमाः पृथिव्याम् ।\nकच्चिन्मानं तात लभन्त एते\nधनुर्भृतः कच्चिदेतेऽप्यरोगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those very wise ones, expert in all the scriptures, the foremost bowmen on earth, do they receive honor, and are they free of illness?"}},{"n":12,"text":"सर्वे कुरुभ्यः स्पृहयन्ति संजय\nधनुर्धरा ये पृथिव्यां युवानः ।\nयेषां राष्ट्रे निवसति दर्शनीयो\nमहेष्वासः शीलवान्द्रोणपुत्रः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the young archers on earth long for the Kurus, in whose kingdom lives Drona's son, the handsome, virtuous great archer."}},{"n":13,"text":"वैश्यापुत्रः कुशली तात कच्चि-\nन्महाप्राज्ञो राजपुत्रो युयुत्सुः ।\nकर्णोऽमात्यः कुशली तात कच्चि-\nत्सुयोधनो यस्य मन्दो विधेयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Is the son of the Vaishya woman, the very wise prince Yuyutsu, well? Is Karna, the minister, well, whom foolish Suyodhana obeys?"}},{"n":14,"text":"स्त्रियो वृद्धा भारतानां जनन्यो\nमहानस्यो दासभार्याश्च सूत ।\nवध्वः पुत्रा भागिनेया भगिन्यो\nदौहित्रा वा कच्चिदप्यव्यलीकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the old women who are mothers of the Bharatas, the cooks, the servants' wives, the daughters-in-law, sons, nephews, sisters and daughters' sons, are they free from harm?"}},{"n":15,"text":"कच्चिद्राजा ब्राह्मणानां यथाव-\nत्प्रवर्तते पूर्ववत्तात वृत्तिम् ।\nकच्चिद्दायान्मामकान्धार्तराष्ट्रो\nद्विजातीनां संजय नोपहन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Does the king treat Brahmins properly, as before? Does Dhritarashtra's son not take away the grants I made to the twice-born, Sanjaya?"}},{"n":16,"text":"कच्चिद्राजा धृतराष्ट्रः सपुत्र\nउपेक्षते ब्राह्मणातिक्रमान्वै ।\nकच्चिन्न हेतोरिव वर्त्मभूत\nउपेक्षते तेषु स न्यूनवृत्तिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Does King Dhritarashtra with his sons not overlook offenses against Brahmins? Does he not, as though just a path, overlook their ill treatment?"}},{"n":17,"text":"एतज्ज्योतिरुत्तमं जीवलोके\nशुक्लं प्रजानां विहितं विधात्रा ।\nते चेल्लोभं न नियच्छन्ति मन्दाः\nकृत्स्नो नाशो भविता कौरवाणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the supreme light in the world of the living, the white light set by the Creator for creatures; if those fools do not restrain greed, the Kauravas will wholly perish."}},{"n":18,"text":"कच्चिद्राजा धृतराष्ट्रः सपुत्रो\nबुभूषते वृत्तिममात्यवर्गे ।\nकच्चिन्न भेदेन जिजीविषन्ति\nसुहृद्रूपा दुर्हृदश्चैकमित्राः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Does King Dhritarashtra with his sons wish to deal fairly with his group of ministers? Do those who look like friends but are foes, with one master, not try to live by creating division?"}},{"n":19,"text":"कच्चिन्न पापं कथयन्ति तात\nते पाण्डवानां कुरवः सर्व एव ।\nकच्चिद्दृष्ट्वा दस्युसंघान्समेता-\nन्स्मरन्ति पार्थस्य युधां प्रणेतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do all the Kurus not speak ill of the Pandavas? Seeing assembled bands of robbers, do they remember Partha, the leader in battles?"}},{"n":20,"text":"मौर्वीभुजाग्रप्रहितान्स्म तात\nदोधूयमानेन धनुर्धरेण ।\nगाण्डीवमुक्तान्स्तनयित्नुघोषा-\nनजिह्मगान्कच्चिदनुस्मरन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do they remember, Sanjaya, those straight arrows loosed from the bowstring's reach, shaken by the archer, released from Gandiva with sounds like thunder?"}},{"n":21,"text":"न ह्यपश्यं कंचिदहं पृथिव्यां\nश्रुतं समं वाधिकमर्जुनेन ।\nयस्यैकषष्टिर्निशितास्तीक्ष्णधाराः\nसुवाससः संमतो हस्तवापः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have not seen or heard of anyone on earth equal or superior to Arjuna, whose sixty-one sharp arrows, honored and fair-feathered, are held in his hand."}},{"n":22,"text":"गदापाणिर्भीमसेनस्तरस्वी\nप्रवेपयञ्शत्रुसंघाननीके ।\nनागः प्रभिन्न इव नड्वलासु\nचङ्क्रम्यते कच्चिदेनं स्मरन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do they remember Bhimasena, quick, mace in hand, making enemy groups tremble in the army, striding like an elephant in rut in reed ponds?"}},{"n":23,"text":"माद्रीपुत्रः सहदेवः कलिङ्गा-\nन्समागतानजयद्दन्तकूरे ।\nवामेनास्यन्दक्षिणेनैव यो वै\nमहाबलं कच्चिदेनं स्मरन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do they remember Sahadeva, son of Madri, who at Dantakura defeated the assembled Kalingas, who shoots with both left hand and right, of great strength?"}},{"n":24,"text":"उद्यन्नयं नकुलः प्रेषितो वै\nगावल्गणे संजय पश्यतस्ते ।\nदिशं प्रतीचीं वशमानयन्मे\nमाद्रीसुतं कच्चिदेनं स्मरन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Charioteer, do they remember Nakula, son of Madri, whom I sent forth in your sight, Sanjaya son of Gavalgana, and who brought the western region under my control?"}},{"n":25,"text":"अभ्याभवो द्वैतवने य आसी-\nद्दुर्मन्त्रिते घोषयात्रागतानाम् ।\nयत्र मन्दाञ्शत्रुवशं प्रयाता-\nनमोचयद्भीमसेनो जयश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do they remember the setback in Dvaitavana when those who came for the cowherds' outing, ill-advised, fell into enemy power, and Bhimasena and Jaya freed the fools?"}},{"n":26,"text":"अहं पश्चादर्जुनमभ्यरक्षं\nमाद्रीपुत्रौ भीमसेनश्च चक्रे ।\nगाण्डीवभृच्छत्रुसंघानुदस्य\nस्वस्त्यागमत्कच्चिदेनं स्मरन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do they remember that afterwards I protected Arjuna, and the sons of Madri and Bhimasena did their part, and the bearer of Gandiva returned safe, having thrown back the enemy groups?"}},{"n":27,"text":"न कर्मणा साधुनैकेन नूनं\nकर्तुं शक्यं भवतीह संजय ।\nसर्वात्मना परिजेतुं वयं चे-\nन्न शक्नुमो धृतराष्ट्रस्य पुत्रम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surely, Sanjaya, one good deed alone is not enough to achieve it; if we cannot conquer Dhritarashtra's son by every means."}}]}]}